  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In first step, acetylation of aniline&nbsp;occurs. This process is done to lower the activating nature of amine otherwise poly substitution will occur.</p><p>On bromination, bromine group is directed at para position. In ortho&nbsp;position repulsion will dominate due to which its percentage of ortho product is less.&nbsp; <img src=\"assets\\st0090_1ea0a8c48573.png\" style=\"width: 901px; height: 231px;\" /></p>"
